  "body": "# Description\r\n\r\nmy server is configured as follows:\r\n\r\n```yml\r\nlisteners:\r\n  - port: 8448\r\n    tls: false\r\n    type: http\r\n    x_forwarded: true\r\n    resources:\r\n      - names: [client, federation]\r\n        compress: false\r\n```\r\n\r\nmy reverse proxy maps `my.host.com:443` / `https://my.host.com` => `8448`. it seems the system & federationtester.matrix.org demands that my federation requests go thru :8448, vs :443.\r\n\r\nthis is a bummer, because i'm serving federation resources off of :443.  the current recipe demands either:\r\n\r\n- configuring a .well-known workflow, which is undesirable--my reverse-proxy configures this and is a blackbox\r\n- using a SRV record, which i can't do, because my (sub)domains all have CNAMEs\r\n\r\n# Discussion\r\n\r\nis there a story around a single port for all traffic?\r\n\r\n",
